      "side": 1,
      "message": "Would you mind moving `PTC_NATIVE_MAPS` and `page_table_check_nr_maps()` into a new `mm/p3s/page_table_check.h`, as `mm/p3s/process_vm_access.h` does for `mm/process_vm_access.c`? The header\u0027s single `#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE` block would also replace the `IS_ENABLED()`. Something like:\n\n```\n#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64_PER_PROCESS_PAGE_SIZE\n#define P3S_PTC_NATIVE_MAPS\tP3S_SLICES_PER_PAGE\n#else\n#define P3S_PTC_NATIVE_MAPS\t1\n#endif\n\n/*\n * Anon mappings are counted in 4KB slices: a native PTE, PMD or PUD maps\n * all slices of each page, a PTE of a 4KB process maps one.\n */\nstatic inline unsigned int p3s_ptc_nr_maps(const struct mm_struct *mm)\n{\n\treturn mm_is_p3s_4k(mm) ? 1 : P3S_PTC_NATIVE_MAPS;\n}\n```\n\n`mm/page_table_check.c` would then just include `\"p3s/page_table_check.h\"` and pass the charge, e.g.:\n\n```\n\t\tpage_table_check_clear(pte_pfn(pte), PAGE_SIZE \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT,\n\t\t\t\t       p3s_ptc_nr_maps(mm));\n```\n\nIf both branches of `__page_table_check_ptes_set()` passed `p3s_ptc_nr_maps(mm)` too, it would be obvious that set and clear charge the same. I think the `nr_maps` argument itself is the smallest hook, since `page_table_check_set()` and `page_table_check_clear()` work on `struct page_table_check`, which is private to this file.",
